   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs ending in -er and -ir",
     "texto": [
      "They are almost regular. **Comer**: como, comes, come, comemos, comem. **Beber**: bebo, bebes, bebe, bebemos, bebem.",
      "The verbs ending in **-ir** only change in the «we» form: **abrir** → abro, abres, abre, abr**i**mos, abrem."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reflexive verbs: the pronoun goes after",
     "texto": [
      "This is one of the big differences with English. In a normal affirmative sentence, the pronoun goes **after** the verb, joined with a **hyphen**: **levanto-me** (I get up), **deito-me** (I go to bed), **visto-me** (I get dressed).",
      "But it goes **before** the verb if there is a negation or a question word: **Não me levanto** cedo. **A que horas te levantas?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
